.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-SIGN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-sign
.Nd sign a file with ML-DSA or SLH-DSA
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis sign
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl o Ar sig
.Op Fl c Ar ctx
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl -ph Ar hash
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis sign
signs the bytes of
.Ar file
with the secret key in
.Ar key
and writes the raw signature (the FIPS 204 or FIPS 205 encoding, no
header) to
.Ar sig ,
by default
.Ar file Ns Pa .sig .
It prints nothing on success.
.Ar file
may be
.Ql -
for standard input, and then
.Fl o
is required.
.Pp
Signing is hedged by default: fresh randomness from the operating system
is mixed into each signature, so two signatures of one file differ.
.Pp
When the public key file
.Ar key Ns .pub
is beside the secret key, the new signature is checked with it before
anything is written: a signature that does not verify (a public key that
is not the pair of
.Ar key ,
or a fault while signing) is not written and the exit status is 2.
Without that file the signature is written unchecked.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
A secret signature key file
.Pq Ql noqtis-key-1 <alg> sec .
A KEM key is refused.
.It Fl o Ar sig , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar sig
Where to write the signature.
.It Fl c Ar ctx , Fl -ctx Ns = Ns Ar ctx
The FIPS 204/205 context string: the bytes of the argument, at most 255.
The same context must be given to
.Xr noqtis-verify 1 .
Default: empty.
.It Fl d , Fl -det
Deterministic signing: the per-signature randomness is all zero (32 bytes
for ML-DSA, n bytes for SLH-DSA), so the same key, file and options give
the same signature.
.It Fl -ph Ar hash
The pre-hash variant (HashML-DSA, HashSLH-DSA): the file is hashed with
.Ar hash
and the digest is signed together with the hash's identifier.
.Ar hash
is one of
.Cm sha224 sha256 sha384 sha512 sha512-224 sha512-256
.Cm sha3-224 sha3-256 sha3-384 sha3-512 shake128 shake256 .
A pre-hash signature verifies only with the same
.Fl -ph .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing signature file.
.El
.Pp
A file over 1 GiB is refused.
A file that is a capsule manifest
.Pq Pa noqtis.json
is signed as given, with a warning: a plain signature is never a seal
.Pq seals are made with their own context ; see Xr noqtis-capsule 5 ,
so to seal a folder use
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on a usage error, a context over 255 bytes, an unknown
pre-hash, a key that is not a secret signature key, an existing
.Ar sig
without
.Fl -force ,
or a file that cannot be read or written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me
ML-DSA-65 key pair: me (secret), me.pub (public)
$ noqtis sign -k me report.pdf
$ noqtis verify -p me.pub -s report.pdf.sig report.pdf
report.pdf: OK (ML-DSA-65)
.Ed
.Pp
With a context string, deterministically, and from standard input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis sign -k me -c release-2026 -d -o notes.sig - < notes.txt
$ noqtis verify -p me.pub -s notes.sig -c release-2026 notes.txt
notes.txt: OK (ML-DSA-65)
.Ed
.Pp
HashML-DSA with SHA-512:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis sign -k me --ph sha512 -o big.sig big.tar
$ noqtis verify -p me.pub -s big.sig --ph sha512 big.tar
big.tar: OK (ML-DSA-65)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-verify 1 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
